      "math_academy_id": "q-108307",
      "sequence_position": 6,
      "problem": "The table below gives the values of $x$ that satisfy $P(X\\ge x)=p,$ where $X∼{χ}^{2}(k).$ Given that $X∼{χ}^{2}(9),$ find the value of $x$ such that $P(X\\le x)=0.05.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.995$ | $0.990$ | $0.975$ | $0.950$ | $0.900$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $7$ | $\\,0.989\\,$ | $\\,1.239\\,$ | $\\,1.690\\,$ | $\\,2.167\\,$ | $\\,2.833\\,$ |\n| $8$ | $\\,1.344\\,$ | $\\,1.646\\,$ | $\\,2.180\\,$ | $\\,2.733\\,$ | $\\,3.490\\,$ |\n| $9$ | $\\,1.735\\,$ | $\\,2.088\\,$ | $\\,2.700\\,$ | $\\,3.325\\,$ | $\\,4.168\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The table shows probabilities in the form $P(X>x).$ So first, we express the desired probability in this form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>x) & =1-P(X\\le x) \\\\  & =1-0.05 \\\\  & =0.95\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $X∼{χ}^{2}(9),$ we focus on the row of the table that corresponds to $k=9.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.995$ | $0.990$ | $0.975$ | $0.950$ | $0.900$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $9$ | $\\,1.735\\,$ | $\\,2.088\\,$ | $\\,2.700\\,$ | $\\,3.325\\,$ | $\\,4.168\\,$ |\n\nFrom this row, we see that\n\n$$\nP(X>3.325)=0.950.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our answer is $x=3.325.$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
